\alias{LearnerCptFeatureless}
\title{Featureless Changepoint Learner}
\description{
A baseline that ignores the sequences and learns a single constant penalty
\code{log(lambda)} for all of them, the one with the fewest label errors summed
over the training sequences.

At train time, the segment path is fitted per sequence and scored against its
label regions. Each model is selected on an interval of \code{log(lambda)}, so the
total label error is a step function of a constant penalty; the learner
evaluates it on every step and keeps the minimum. When several steps reach
it, the middle one of them is taken, and the penalty returned is the midpoint
of that step (or one unit past the outermost breakpoint for an unbounded
step). Sequences without labels do not affect the fit.

At predict time, the learner returns \code{response}, the learned constant
\code{log(lambda)}, for every sequence. A learner that uses features is only worth
its features if it beats this baseline, e.g. in \code{\link[mlr3:benchmark]{mlr3::benchmark()}}.

The label solvers are chosen by the task's \code{label_type}:
\code{"changepoint"} uses \code{\link[changepoint:cpt.mean]{changepoint::cpt.mean()}}, \code{"peak"} uses
\code{\link[PeakSegOptimal:PeakSegPDPAchrom]{PeakSegOptimal::PeakSegPDPAchrom()}}.
}
